>
>blah blah blah (end of previous message)
>
>>From:brianh@netins.net..(complete headers and valid messages follows)
>
>If you just go in and delete the top few lines until you get a valid from
>line you are ok.  Has anyone else seen anything like this ever happending?
>We are running 4.0B, Qpopper2.4.  This happends after a user downloads a
>message and then clears it from the server.  It does not have anything to
>do with incoming, because in a few cases we have seen just the end of a
>letter and no from line.
>


Most everyone said that they had experienced the same problems with
different qpopper versions.  On monday I moved to ipop3d, which seemed to
work better.  Unfortunatly we have a system where sometimes people use pop
clients and sometimes they use mh/pine.  Ipop3d inserts a "control"
message at the top of all mail folders, which is then incorporated with
mh/pine, but not pop clients.  So last night I had to explain to 10,000
people why they got a message of "Do NOT delete this message" from our
servers.  Ipop also appears to have a memory leak that crashes our system
after about 2 hours of heavy use.

I am now trying to compile other pop servers to test them (very little
luck, ideas on different servers?).

--Brian

