>            (for example running 'make-ssh-known-hosts')

Nope.  If a host is not in the known-hosts file ssh just asks
if you want to add it and then proceeds if you answer yes.
This only happens the first time you try to access a new host
so it's no problem unless you're adding a lot of new hosts.


Ian

