Thanks to (in no particular order): Brian Leverson
                                    Gyula Szokoly
                                    Penny Champine
                                    Allan Simeone
                                    Serge Munhoven

A number of things needed to be done to properly configure the NFS server
on the VMS box: I needed to create a proxy for the unix box, with UID and
GID of -2, needed to map the filesystems under UCX (which I'd done), and
needed to export them (which I hadn't done).  All is well after much
tweaking. 

Other options which I didn't explore or exploit fully were: install
vbackup on the Unix box, install xdir on the Unix box (which I ended up
doing anyway), and install Multinet for VMS as a TCP/IP stack.

A summary of responses is included below.

--Don

----------------
Don,

Get hold of the "OpenVMS & DEC OSF/1 Interoperability Tools" CD, dated 
September 1994, part no. AG-QBX6A-XE.  A program named 'vbackup' allows 
restoration of VMS savesets to Unix.  

