Date: Tue, 16 Jun 1998 14:51:41 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] maxuprcc
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078712011684

Dear Gurus,

My problem: all of a sudden, a user can't log in and gets the
             message: 
task_create() failed for pid 4368: maxuprc (=128) exceeded for uid 266.


Thanks to: Giorgio Pastore, Bernt Christandl, Mireille BOF,
           Martin Moore, Nathan Grass, Susan Rodriguez,
           Stephane E. Fernandez,

I could better see where to fumble in.

They all recommended to check the current value of maxuprc (it was
what I expected) and check for the user's processes with a command
like "ps -U userid"

This made it (the 128 processes owned by the poor user were not
displayed by "ps aux", hence my confusion) and I could understand 
what happened: a loop in one of his scripts.

I killed the offending processes (kill -9) and corrected the script.

Thanks!

Jean-Loup

