To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY - Problems with Exceed on DU3.2g with C2
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078712011671

The original posting follows the solution.
To fix the problem do the following.

Just edit /etc/auth/system/ttys and /etc/auth/system/devassign creating
lines appropriated to your microcomputer emulating X terminal. Something
like 

machine\:0|machine\:0.0:t_devname=machine\:0:t_uid=user:t_logtime#841060342:\
        :t_unsuctime#839963102:t_xdisplay:t_login_timeout#0:chkent:

and

machine\:0:v_devs=machine\:0:v_type=xdisplay:chkent:

respectively, where "machine" is your microcomputer name defined in the 
DNS server.

Thank you very much to Oyanarte Portilho for this solution.
Thanks also to the following who also replied with similar suggestions.

lombardi emanuele
Martin Mokrejs
richard n. frank
Nathan Grass

Just as an addition, fixing this problem unearthed another which was, after
logging in, I got the message

 Cannot start session manager from remote client -- access denied

The solution to this was provided by Hummingbird here in Oz, the solution is to
make sure the following things are setup in the Xconfig section of Exceed.

Communication - set the startup mode to XDMCP-broadcast
Security - check the Allow Clients To Modify Host Access Control List
Protocol - check the DECwindows Compatibility

Thanks again to everyone for their help, this list is certainly an excellent
resource.
Glenn

