To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: need hint for new installation of DUX and preserving the
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078712011598

Hello,

because of hardware and DUX update I had to preserve my current
Pathworks Configuration and
restore them after the fresh install. 

Thanks to MC.Vialatte@cust.univ-bpclermont.fr  and Charles Vachon
[cvachon@mrn.gouv.qc.ca]
how responded and directed me in the right direction. They suggested to
deinstall (setld -d  ) all 
Pathworks subsets and you will be asked to save the current
configuration. Further installations
will ask you for including these configuration files. 

Unfortunately I didn't work for me - the fresh installation told me
something about corrupt files
and I should correct the problems manualy. But see how I succeeded:

- stop the pathworks and license (if running) daemons
- save all from /var/net/servers (I used simply tar) (and if needed
/var/spool/lpd for printers)
- save /etc/passwd, group, printcap and lprsetup.dat
- make your system changes ( I installed a new raid and DUX 4.0d)
- install a fresh Pathworks as you had running before, stop it
- copy the saved /etc/* and /var/net/* and /var/spool/* back to your new
system
- reboot the machine and you will see a running pathworks with all your
shares, users, printers
  and so on

best regards and thank you very much!
