From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Jun 05 19:28:52 1998
From: Charles Vachon <cvachon () mrn ! gouv ! qc ! ca>
Date: Fri, 05 Jun 1998 19:28:52 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: usermod/useradd defaults
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078712011491

Original posting:

>Hello all,
>
>I would like to know where do the usermod/useradd commands take their
>default values from. Since these defaults can be modified, I assume there
>must be a file somewhere holding them. The usermod man page states "The
>usermod command operates on the appropriate files for the specific level of
>system security", which is rather uninformative... Maybe I missed something
>else in the documentation?
>
>Any pointers would be greatly appreciated.
>
>

I did not receive a single response on this one! But, I just found the
answer myself, by sheer luck, so I thought of putting up this summary, just
in case someone else ever needs this information.

The default values of the usermod/useradd commands are taken from the files
$HOME/.sysman/Account_defaults and $HOME/.sysman/UserAccount_defaults of
the root account.



