Thank you all for your time.

Well it sounds like mt isn't acting odd at all.  It did just what I told it to 
do.  When I told it to use the rmt1h device it opened the device, went to the 
the next save set.  Closed the device and, sence it was not the non-rewind 
device rewinded the tape.

I should have told it to use the non rewind device /dev/nrmt1h.  It must take 
the /dev/nrmt0h device by default.  I've never seen this issue with just the 
"mt fsf 1" command.

It was also suggested that I go home and get some rest; I've forwarded this to 
my manager -- who has the interpersonal skills of Cligula (sp).

